<title>EGYPT: Egyptian pound average interbank rates rise.</title>
<headline>Egyptian pound average interbank rates rise.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound rose on Wednesday to between 10-1/16 and 10-1/4 percent from Tuesday's 10-1/8 percent in a slightly liquid private-sector market, bankers said.</p>
<p>One-week rates also rose to a range of between 10-1/8 and 10-3/8 percent from 10-1/4 percent, the bankers added.</p>
<p>State-owned banks kept their minimum interbank lending rate at 10-1/2 percent, they said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
